No speculative extensions or new physical entities are to be introduced unless strictly required for internal consistency. Development will focus on reinterpreting well-understood physical phenomena, postponing the treatment of anomalies and open questions until the framework for known physics is fully established and validated.

\subsection*{2. Strategic Rationale for Strict Framing}

The choice to adopt a single strict frame during development is made for reasons of:
\begin{itemize}
